From f6c4762bdca554050b1c31f345a30aa1990eb22f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel FORTE <2580288+g4bwy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:10:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [Perf][Qwen4Exp] Score dense FP8 linears as W8A8 int8 on
 sm_80

sm_80 has no FP8 tensor cores, so Qwen4Exp's dense linears (attention
qkv/o, GDN projections, dense and shared MLP) run bf16 GEMMs on
dequantized weights. A W8A8 shootout on this box measures CUTLASS int8
at 1.29-1.68x over that path at the production prefill chunk (M=2048),
per-token activation quant included, with int8 losing only below ~2M
weight elements or K<1024.

VLLM_QWEN4EXP_DENSE_W8A8=1 (default off) walks the model once and swaps
the quant method of per-tensor-FP8 dense linears to a subclass that
round-trips the effective bf16 weight to per-output-channel int8 once
at process_weights_after_loading - before the FP8 kernel rewrites the
weight in place - then scores prefill-sized batches with dynamic
per-token quant plus cutlass_scaled_mm. Everything else keeps today's
path: decode batches below M=512 (inside the capture range), block
quant, static activation scales, bias, MoE experts (grouped int8 loses
on this box), batch-invariant mode, other architectures, and every GPU
but sm_80.

The int8 cache lives next to the FP8 weight so the fallback stays
live; costs a few GB on the last stage, listed for boot verification.
